  "L06-L48. Checked: the increments are those of seven months of 207 days, 29 days and 6 hours; with Brahmagupta's parameters (p. 42, JP2 0074) 207 days give the sun 204° 1′ 12″, the moon 207° 30′ 20″, its anomaly 184° 27′ 14″, the node 10° 58′ 17″; 29 days 28° 34′ 57″, 22° 6′ 52″, 18° 53′ 5″, 1° 32′ 13″; 6 hours 14′ 47″, 3° 17′ 39″, 3° 15′ 58″, 48″. For the node the 29 years of the table, 184° 41′ 57″, are 8″ more than these parameters give (184° 41′ 49″) and than the 184° 42′ of p. 59 (JP2 0091, L26), rounded. With the count of p. 42 (JP2 0074, L22-L27), where noon of 15 Ṣafar is 1 month and 14 days after the end of the year, 7 months, 29 days and 6 hours lead to 6 in the evening of 30 Shaʿbān; the evening that ends 29 Shaʿbān would be 28 days and 6 hours. The equations of Table 24, 1° 57′ 35″ and 4° 48′ 29″, are to be compared with the table.",
